turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"id\":\"QL-26\",\"points\":[{\"point\":1,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Must state that the ETF keeps a record for each basket exchanged with an authorized participant. The record must cover at least three things. (a) It must identify each holding in the basket by identifier or description, with its quantity and/or percentage weight. (b) It must include the identity of the transacting AP. (c) It must include at least one of two items: the cash balancing amount (if any), or, where applicable, the custom-basket designation together with a record that the custom basket complies with the ETF's custom-basket policies and procedures. Full credit for this bundled point requires all elements: holdings identification, quantity/weight, the custom-basket designation and compliance statement where applicable, the cash balancing amount, and AP identity. Half credit applies if the answer gives only generic 'basket composition/holdings' records, or omits two or more of the listed elements. Optional subdetails: specific identifier types such as ticker symbol or CUSIP; that the cash balancing amount is recorded 'if any'; that the compliance statement references policies under Rule 6c-11(c)(3).\"},{\"point\":2,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Must state that the exchanged-basket records are kept for at least five years, with the first two years in an easily or readily accessible place. Half credit applies if the answer gives the five-year period but omits the two-year accessibility tier, or gives the accessibility tier without a clear overall period. A wrong number of years for either tier is not partial; see central_errors.\"},{\"point\":3,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Must state that the ETF keeps all written authorized participant agreements, or copies of them, for at least five years, with the first two years easily accessible. Stating that the same five-year/two-year period applies to both record categories satisfies the period portion. Half credit applies if the answer mentions keeping AP agreements but gives no retention period, or applies the period only to basket records without extending it to AP agreements. Optional subdetails: the agreement may be with the ETF or with one of its service providers (e.g., distributor/transfer agent) and allows the AP to place purchase/redemption orders. Graders should not penalize an answer for content missing from the bank prose; this point is an accepted source supplement based on Rule 6c-11(d)(1).\"}],\"central_errors\":[\"States a total retention period other than at least five years, e.g. three or six years, or 'for the life of the fund' as the stated minimum.\",\"States an easily or readily accessible period other than the first two years, e.g. the first year or all five years.\",\"Asserts that AP agreements need not be retained or are exempt from Rule 6c-11(d), or that basket records need not be retained.\",\"Asserts that the Rule 6c-11(d) obligation is met by public website disclosure or by filing with the SEC instead of preservation by the ETF.\",\"Asserts that the custom-basket compliance record is required for every basket, including non-custom ones. Also wrong: asserting that the transacting AP's identity is not recorded.\",\"Attributes these retention requirements to a materially different and contradictory regime as the governing rule, e.g. claiming Rule 6c-11 imposes no recordkeeping and only Rule 31a-2 periods apply with different durations.\"],\"scoring_rule\":{\"correct\":\"All three required points meet their minimums with no central error. Points 2 and 3 may be satisfied by a single statement that both record types are kept for at least five years, the first two easily accessible. Score 1.0.\",\"partial\":\"No central error, but at least one required point is missing or only partially covered. Score proportionally: each required point counts 1/3. A point meeting only its half-credit criteria earns half of its share. Typical partial scores: basket elements and retention correct but AP agreements omitted = 0.67; generic basket composition plus a correct five/two-year period for both record types = about 0.83. Omission alone never makes an answer wrong.\",\"wrong\":\"Contains any central error regarding a required element, or covers none of the three required points at least at the half-credit level. Score 0.\"}}\n```","ttft_ms":9835,"type":"result","duration_ms":23022,"uuid":"6d5eedd1-fa62-4288-ae94-b4a61c8f3a13","ttft_stream_ms":677,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":677,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
